  "description": "v031's exact recipe with ONE change: AdamW weight_decay 0.01 -> 0.03. Model, teacher, distill_weight, schedule, LR and seed all unchanged.",
  "hypothesis": "A direct test of the DIAGNOSIS behind three failed capacity runs. Bigger models lost monotonically -- head -3.2 sigma, hidden 285 -13.7, hidden 415 -21.7. The standard reading is that extra capacity here is absorbed as overfitting rather than used. If that reading is right, more regularisation should HELP at the current size, and we have never tested it: weight_decay has sat at 0.01 and dropout at 0.0 since v011.\n\n  This is the one experiment that could make the capacity results look different rather than just confirming them. If heavier decay improves 225,922 params, then the trunk widenings were unregularised rather than wrong, and v026/v027 might be recoverable. If it does nothing, the capacity losses were not an overfitting signature at all and the diagnosis in those three commit messages is wrong.\n\n  3x is large enough to see an effect and small enough to stay in the regime AdamW handles well. dropout is deliberately NOT also changed -- two knobs at once would make a null unreadable.",
  "change_vs_parent": "optim.weight_decay 0.01 -> 0.03 only. dropout stays 0.0 so this isolates the decay term.",
